  "raw_response": "{\"status\":\"answered\",\"points\":[{\"text\":\"refusal_correctness 的跨模型极差为 0.478–0.870，即 39 个百分点（0–1 量表）。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E1\",\"quote\":\"The largest cross-provider spread sits in refusal_correctness (0.478–0.870, a 39-point gap on a 0–1 scale)\"}]},{\"text\":\"section_coverage 的跨模型极差为 0.636–0.955，即 32 个百分点。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E1\",\"quote\":\"section_coverage (0.636–0.955, a 32-point gap)\"}]},{\"text\":\"factual_accuracy 的跨模型极差为 4.745–5.000，在 1–5 量表上仅 0.255 分。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E1\",\"quote\":\"factual_accuracy (4.745–5.000, a 0.255-point gap on a 1–5 scale)\"}]},{\"text\":\"completeness 的跨模型极差为 4.571–4.980，仅 0.409 分。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E2\",\"quote\":\"completeness (4.571–4.980, a 0.409-point gap)\"}]},{\"text\":\"作者认为 citation-grounding 指标具有区分度，而 evaluator 指标基本饱和。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E1\",\"quote\":\"The citation-grounding metrics discriminate; the evaluator metrics largely saturate.\"}]},{\"text\":\"作者将这种差异解读为：模型在数据集所涉事实性论断上普遍正确，但在引用哪些证据以及这些证据是否可验证方面差异很大，而这正是引用指标意在揭示的区别。\",\"citations\":[{\"id\":\"E2\",\"quote\":\"We read this as “current-generation models are uniformly correct on the\\n\\nkinds of factual claims the dataset asks about, but they vary substantially in which evidence they choose to cite and whether that evidence is verifiable” — exactly the distinction the citation metrics were designed to\\nexpose.\"}]}],\"limitations\":[\"提供的证据只覆盖了摘要或结果部分的相关段落，未覆盖完整方法或结论，也未说明这些差距的统计显著性。\"]}",
